{"id":"09-code-review","number":9,"slug":"reviewing-agent-code","title":"Reviewing agent code","short":"Reviewing agent code","module":"Working with one agent","summary":"Agents write code faster than anyone can read it, and review has become the new bottleneck. Practitioners disagree about reading every line, but they agree on how to review well: scale depth to blast radius, review your own work first, use a fresh-context reviewer, and turn repeated comments into rules.","voice":"Eric","scenes":[{"template":"title","chapter":"Intro","narration":"Agents can write code far faster than any human can read it. So who reviews it, and how much is enough? This is where agentic engineering gets hard.","params":{"kicker":"Lesson 9","module":"Module 2 · Working with one agent","title":"Reviewing *agent code*","subtitle":"Review has become the new bottleneck. Here's how to scale it.","bubble":"Here's 2,000 lines. Enjoy!","mood":"happy"},"start":0.5,"dur":11.388,"words":[{"text":"Agents","s":0.8,"e":1.2},{"text":"can","s":1.28,"e":1.36},{"text":"write","s":1.44,"e":1.68},{"text":"code","s":1.76,"e":2.08},{"text":"far","s":2.24,"e":2.48},{"text":"faster","s":2.56,"e":2.96},{"text":"than","s":3.08,"e":3.2},{"text":"any","s":3.28,"e":3.44},{"text":"human","s":3.52,"e":3.84},{"text":"can","s":3.92,"e":4},{"text":"read","s":4.08,"e":4.24},{"text":"it.","s":4.32,"e":4.72},{"text":"So","s":4.96,"e":5.2},{"text":"who","s":5.44,"e":5.6},{"text":"reviews","s":5.8,"e":6},{"text":"it,","s":6.08,"e":6.48},{"text":"and","s":6.6,"e":6.72},{"text":"how","s":6.88,"e":6.96},{"text":"much","s":7.04,"e":7.2},{"text":"is","s":7.24,"e":7.28},{"text":"enough?","s":7.36,"e":7.84},{"text":"This","s":8.4,"e":8.56},{"text":"is","s":8.64,"e":8.72},{"text":"where","s":8.8,"e":8.88},{"text":"agentic","s":9,"e":9.44},{"text":"engineering","s":9.72,"e":10},{"text":"gets","s":10.12,"e":10.24},{"text":"hard.","s":10.32,"e":11.04}]},{"template":"stat","chapter":"The new bottleneck","narration":"At Uber, the time